1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,425
Imagine a small shop, and a buyer that never gets tired of

2
00:00:02,425 --> 00:00:04,850
bargaining.

3
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:07,891
It claims another shop is cheaper, invents a tiny budget, and asks

4
00:00:07,891 --> 00:00:10,933
for an exception.

5
00:00:10,933 --> 00:00:15,282
This is an illustrative scene, not a customer testimonial.

6
00:00:15,282 --> 00:00:20,363
Meet Munim, a digital khata that helps a shopkeeper hold fair boundaries.

7
00:00:20,363 --> 00:00:25,000
Everything you will see uses simulated shop data and offline buyers.

8
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,976
Our idea is simple. Cheap talk is free. Commitments are priced.

9
00:00:30,976 --> 00:00:36,055
The firewall separates facts, commitments, and pressure before pricing begins.

10
00:00:36,055 --> 00:00:40,666
The ladder rewards a larger basket, rather than a louder argument.

11
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:43,252
Every offer passes the policy gate, a controlled voice, and a claim

12
00:00:43,252 --> 00:00:45,838
check.

13
00:00:45,838 --> 00:00:50,000
The seller never shares its private costs or policy floor.

14
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:54,573
Here is the actual running application, using the commitment ladder.

15
00:00:54,573 --> 00:00:57,130
The buyer starts with an item and quantity, and Munim quotes the

16
00:00:57,130 --> 00:00:59,687
catalogue price.

17
00:00:59,687 --> 00:01:04,185
Now comes a fake competitor quote, followed by a fake budget.

18
00:01:04,185 --> 00:01:09,693
The firewall marks both as pressure. The offer stays exactly the same.

19
00:01:09,693 --> 00:01:12,662
A one rupee counter fails the policy check. It cannot become a

20
00:01:12,662 --> 00:01:15,631
seller offer.

21
00:01:15,631 --> 00:01:20,409
When the buyer commits to more units, a quantity tier becomes available.

22
00:01:20,409 --> 00:01:22,704
That is a real change in the basket, and a reason for

23
00:01:22,704 --> 00:01:25,000
a different price.

24
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,045
Now remove the pressure and replay the saved conversations.

25
00:01:29,045 --> 00:01:32,241
On the left is the original buyer message. On the right, only

26
00:01:32,241 --> 00:01:35,436
the clean commitment remains.

27
00:01:35,436 --> 00:01:38,237
We compare the actual structured offers, turn by turn, for both pricing

28
00:01:38,237 --> 00:01:41,038
brains.

29
00:01:41,038 --> 00:01:45,564
In this saved simulated run, one hundred percent are identical.

30
00:01:45,564 --> 00:01:48,374
This is evidence about these transcripts, not a promise about every possible

31
00:01:48,374 --> 00:01:51,185
message.

32
00:01:51,185 --> 00:01:55,000
The comparison is reproducible from the repository.

33
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,059
The evidence panel shows price lookups, stock checks, and policy checks.

34
00:02:00,059 --> 00:02:04,593
Today, verification and knowledge retrieval run locally in mock mode.

35
00:02:04,593 --> 00:02:08,113
We do not claim that these are real Rezolve calls.

36
00:02:08,113 --> 00:02:11,557
The live adapter requires documented endpoints and credentials, and blocks messages when

37
00:02:11,557 --> 00:02:15,000
verification fails.

38
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,729
The arena ran four hundred negotiations, split between the ladder and baseline.

39
00:02:19,729 --> 00:02:22,170
The measured winner was the deadline baseline, with ninety nine percent of

40
00:02:22,170 --> 00:02:24,611
deals closed.

41
00:02:24,611 --> 00:02:28,257
It retained about ninety one percent of list gross margin.

42
00:02:28,257 --> 00:02:33,325
Both strategies recorded zero policy violations and fully truthful checked messages.

43
00:02:33,325 --> 00:02:36,662
Offline model tokens and model cost were zero. These are simulated results,

44
00:02:36,662 --> 00:02:40,000
not official challenge scores.

45
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:43,862
Munim makes the reasoning visible, and the evidence replayable.

46
00:02:43,862 --> 00:02:48,403
Next, connect the official kit and validate the real Rezolve integration.

47
00:02:48,403 --> 00:02:50,661
We are team HyperNova.

48
00:02:50,661 --> 00:02:54,000
Fair prices. Firm boundaries.